// §8c's pathological fixture: "a self-referencing folder hierarchy."
// self-referential-folder.authz's own `folder.parent: folder` makes
// `permission view = viewer | parent->view` genuinely self-referential
// at the schema-graph level — the search's own union-branch computation
// recurses into `folder#view` a second time (via `parent->view`) before
// the simpler `viewer` branch wins, so this exercises the cycle-safety
// code path directly, not just its absence. Deliberately a positive
// control, not a constraint problem: proves §1's own theorem holds for
// a genuinely self-referential schema, not just a linear chain — "cycles
// can always be unrolled zero times," confirmed here by a real search
// run finding the minimal one-tuple witness (a direct `viewer` grant),
// never needing to traverse `parent->view` at all, self-validated
// against the real engine in under 5ms. Expected verdict: VIOLATED.
invariant folder_view_reachable {
  s: user
  o: folder

  goal: view(s, o)
}
